#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
===============================================================================
 NORA INTENT ANALYSIS  v2.1   —   PII-HARDENED
 Turn-level conversation analytics for telecom intent classification
===============================================================================

WHY v2.1 EXISTS
---------------
v2 fixed the masking function but still let customer data reach the report by
going AROUND that function. Three routes were found in the v2 output:

  1. Phase 1's column inventory printed a raw sample of every column, including
     the message body and the internal `_raw` column. That put a real customer
     name, BAN, IMEI and callback number straight into the HTML.
  2. Cluster example text carried names that were pasted into the free-text
     body rather than into a form field, so field-bounded masking never saw
     them ("caller/customername: <several names>").
  3. A before/after sample CSV dumped raw and cleaned text side by side.

v2.1 changes the architecture so that this class of bug cannot recur:

  * NOTHING is written to an output by calling `to_csv` or `to_html` directly.
    Every DataFrame and every string passes through Guard.safe_frame() first.
  * Guard is FAIL-CLOSED. After masking, it re-scans the text. If anything that
    looks like an identifier or a known name survives, the whole cell is
    replaced with [REDACTED] rather than shipped. A missed pattern costs you a
    blanked cell, never a leak.
  * A NAME LEXICON is built from the corpus before anything is written. Every
    value ever seen in a name-type field, anywhere in the file, becomes a
    redaction target everywhere else in the file — including inside free text
    that has no form structure at all. This is what catches route 2.
  * The name lexicon is also injected into the stopword list, so no customer
    name can appear as a cluster top-term or a learned keyword.
  * `_raw` and the source message column are excluded from every output by
    name. The column inventory reports the SHAPE of a column (length, digit
    density, word count), never a sample of its contents.
  * No output contains: customer name, BAN, IMEI, ICCID, EID, MSISDN, callback
    number, email, address, ZIP, lat/long, IP or URL. Identifier-type form
    fields are never emitted as values in any form, masked or otherwise.

ALSO FIXED IN v2.1 (analysis correctness)
-----------------------------------------
  4. Phase 1.6 computed association across ALL rows with the assistant label
     filled in as "__blank__", so the role column scored Cramer's V 0.9999 and
     was reported as "NEAR-DETERMINISTIC - this column effectively IS the
     label". That was an artefact of the blank fill. It is now computed on
     labelled rows only.
  5. The confidence calibration curve collapsed to a single bin and the report
     still printed "confidence is monotonically informative". A single point is
     monotonic by definition. The claim now requires at least three bins.
  6. Cleaning step 4 reported "median 71 chars -> 71 chars" because it read the
     already-filtered frame. The before figure is now captured up front.
  7. The keyword rule block reported only discourse words for the majority
     class. A minimum-classes-covered warning now fires when one class learns
     fewer than a derived floor of indicators, so the weakness is stated rather
     than left for the reader to notice.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 X AND Y
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   X        the customer's problem statement, extracted from the user turn
   y_turn   the per-turn label
   y_global the conversation label
   Assistant turns are never X: they are NORA's answer and contain the
   conclusion. Using them as input would be target leakage.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 RUN
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   pip install pandas numpy scikit-learn scipy matplotlib

   python nora_intent_analysis_v2_1.py --input intent_labels_all_flattened.csv ^
       --outdir nora_out_v2_1 --salt-file C:\\Users\\you\\nora_salt.txt

   Add --no-free-text to strip every free-text column from every output and
   keep only counts, metrics and vocabulary. Use that for anything leaving the
   team.

   Retype the double hyphens by hand; copied ones become en dashes and argparse
   will reject them.
===============================================================================
"""

